{"Title":"An Act designating a certain bridge in the city of Leominster as the Honorable John Walter Olver Memorial Bridge","BillNumber":"S2221","DocketNumber":"SD1949","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"JJC0","Name":"John J. Cronin","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JJC0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T20:43:00.55"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"JJC0","Name":"John J. Cronin","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JJC0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T20:43:00.55"},{"Id":"NMB1","Name":"Natalie M. Blais","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/NMB1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-23T11:01:25.41"},{"Id":"MPK1","Name":"Michael P. Kushmerek","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/MPK1","ResponseDate":"2023-03-16T15:41:55.39"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2221/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. Cronin, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 2221) of John J. Cronin and Natalie M. Blais for legislation to designate a certain bridge in the city of Leominster as the Honorable John Walter Olver Memorial Bridge.  Transportation.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. The \"Twin Cities Rail Trail” Bridge L-08-023 (BX9), in the City of Leominster, constructed over Route 2 in the area of Exit 99B, shall be designated and known as the Honorable John Walter Olver Memorial Bridge in recognition of Congressman John Walter Olver. Congressman Olver served in both chambers of the Massachusetts General Court, being elected to the Massachusetts House of Representatives in 1968, and the Massachusetts Senate in 1972. Congressman Olver represented the 1st Congressional District of Massachusetts from 1991-2013. The Massachusetts Department of Transportation shall erect and maintain a suitable marker bearing the designation in compliance with the standards of the department.\r\n\tSECTION 2. This act shall take effect upon its passage.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J27","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J27"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Place in the OD with Recommended Amendment","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"S29","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/S29"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[{"AmendmentNumber":"1","ParentBillNumber":"S2221","Branch":"Senate","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2221/Branches/Senate/Amendments/1/"}]}